      "content": "19. COMMON ARTICLE CONFUSIONS (HIGH-PROBABILITY SSC AREA)"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "dhl1f6b"
    },
    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Primary vs. Secondary Purpose Trap: Do not use 'the' before school, college, hospital, or church when visited for their primary purpose (e.g., 'He went to hospital for treatment', but 'His father went to the hospital to meet the doctor').",
        "Vowel Sound Exception: Words like 'European', 'University', and 'One-eyed man' take 'a' because they begin with consonant sounds ('yu' and 'wa'), whereas 'Hour' and 'Honest' take 'an'.",
        "Superlatives & Ordinals: Always use 'the' before superlative degrees ('the best') and ordinal numbers ('the first chapter')."
      ],
      "id": "ji2yrtg"
    },
